<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 7 Discussion and Limitations ‣ OpenClaw PRISM: A Zero-Fork, Defense-in-Depth Runtime Security Layer for Tool-Augmented LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Safety properties depend in part on explicit runtime policy, not only on classification.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 7 Discussion and Limitations ‣ OpenClaw PRISM: A Zero-Fork, Defense-in-Depth Runtime Security Layer for Tool-Augmented LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">File and path protections are intentionally scoped.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px4" title="In 7 Discussion and Limitations ‣ OpenClaw PRISM: A Zero-Fork, Defense-in-Depth Runtime Security Layer for Tool-Augmented LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">PRISM is framework-specific by design.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px5" title="In 7 Discussion and Limitations ‣ OpenClaw PRISM: A Zero-Fork, Defense-in-Depth Runtime Security Layer for Tool-Augmented LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">PRISM does not replace lower-layer system hardening.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px6" title="In 7 Discussion and Limitations ‣ OpenClaw PRISM: A Zero-Fork, Defense-in-Depth Runtime Security Layer for Tool-Augmented LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">The current system should not be overinterpreted as production-proven at large scale.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S7.SS1" title="In 7 Discussion and Limitations ‣ OpenClaw PRISM: A Zero-Fork, Defense-in-Depth Runtime Security Layer for Tool-Augmented LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">7.1 </span>Future Directions</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
